---
# The one door that lets daniel-server's Docker otel-collector forward Claude Code
# telemetry into this stack (slice-7 D7, executed early — see
# docs/k3s-migration/slice-7-drain-and-join.md D7 execution record).
#
# WHY A LAN DOOR INTO THE LOOPBACK-ONLY STACK IS ACCEPTABLE HERE: the loopback posture
# protects READ access to stored prompts (Loki/Tempo/Grafana), and none of those gain a
# route. This is a WRITE-ONLY surface — OTLP gRPC ingest on the collector — through which
# nothing stored can be retrieved. Modelled on prometheus-ingressroute.yaml.j2's write
# door, with the same two load-bearing facts: Traefik matches ClientIP against the TCP
# peer (not X-Forwarded-For), and the Traefik Service is externalTrafficPolicy=Local (no
# SNAT), so the /32 guard is real. Same single-sender ClientIP, same no-rate-limit
# reasoning: the sender replays its backlog after an outage, and 429s there mean dropped
# telemetry.
#
# `scheme: h2c` is load-bearing: OTLP/gRPC is HTTP/2, TLS terminates at Traefik, and the
# collector's receiver is plaintext — without h2c Traefik downgrades the backend leg to
# HTTP/1.1 and every gRPC call fails.
#
# LAN-ONLY: does not honour k8s_public_route, and must never follow the app routes public.
# The forwarder and this route both dissolve at the Phase F join, when a collector
# DaemonSet gives daniel-server its own loopback hostPort.
apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
kind: IngressRoute
metadata:
  name: claude-otel-ingest
  namespace: {{ k8s_observability_namespace }}
spec:
  entryPoints:
    - https
  routes:
    - kind: Rule
      match: "Host(`claude-otel-ingest{{ k8s_hostname_suffix }}.local.{{ domain }}`) && ClientIP(`{{ k8s_bridge_client_ip }}/32`)"
      services:
        - name: otel-collector
          port: {{ claude_otel_otlp_port }}
          scheme: h2c
  tls:
    certResolver: cloudflare
    options:
      name: modern
    domains:
      - main: "{{ domain }}"
        sans:
          - "*.{{ domain }}"
          - "*.local.{{ domain }}"
